{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>From the time.</b> Because of the overflowing torrent it will take you." "<b>Terror.</b> It is not like זעוה (Deuteronomy 28:25), inverted when they separate [the letters], but rather it is from the root of ולא זע ממנו (Esther 5:9), and the vav comes in the middle like the vav of מות, and the meaning is that whoever hears the report of you will fear what has happened [n: The Hebrew reads שירע, apparently a scribal error for שאירע ('what has happened to you'); translated accordingly.] to you."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:38.410515975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}